    <!-- ── WHY VERSIONED MEMORY ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section" id="versioned" aria-labelledby="versioned-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Why versioned memory</p>
          <h2 id="versioned-title">Why agents need versioned memory</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="answer">
          An assistant that forgets between sessions loses days of learning. An assistant
          whose memory ignores git state applies experimental rules to production code.
          Muse solves both — and adds a third: every memory carries blame metadata so
          nothing is ever silently corrupted. Muse is <strong>Git for AI memory</strong>:
          it compiles observations into curatable memories, scopes them to your branch,
          and verifies every note against your real code.
        </p>
        <p class="plain">
          <strong>The short version:</strong> memory should work like your source code. Branches isolate experiments, blame traces who wrote what, and rollbacks undo mistakes — not a flat file that everyone edits.
        </p>
